MinVersion TLS 1.2, MaxVersion TLS 1.3 | internal/eval_hub/mlflow/mlflow.go:60-63 |\n216\t| **Crypto libraries** | stdlib crypto/tls (FIPS via OpenSSL at runtime), google.golang.org/grpc/credentials | internal/eval_hub/mlflow/mlflow.go:6, internal/otel/otel_sdk.go |\n217\t| **Certificate handling** | System trust store by default; custom CA bundle via CACertPath configuration for MLflow | internal/eval_hub/mlflow/mlflow.go:66-76 |\n218\t| **Non-FIPS crypto risks** | None detected | Dockerfile.konflux:27 |\n219\t\n220\tThe MLflow HTTP client explicitly sets TLS 1.2 minimum and TLS 1.3 maximum (`mlflow.go:61-62`), and supports loading a custom CA certificate pool when `CACertPath` is configured. The gRPC credentials import is used for the OpenTelemetry OTLP exporter. With `GOEXPERIMENT=strictfipsruntime`, Go's crypto/tls operations are routed through the system OpenSSL at runtime. [source: internal/eval_hub/mlflow/mlflow.go:58-80]\n221\t## Data Flows\n222\t\n223\t- **API request flow:** Clients reach the eval-hub REST API on port 8080. Routes for evaluation jobs, collections, and providers pass through the conditional identity gate (`server.go:430-441`), which enforces X-User and X-Tenant headers when configuration enables it. Health, docs, and OpenAPI endpoints bypass this gate. In cluster mode, Prometheus metrics are served on a dedicated metrics server at port 8081; in local mode, `/metrics` is additionally registered on the main API port. [source: internal/eval_hub/server/server.go:444-488, internal/eval_hub/server/metrics_server.go:23-42, internal/eval_hub/config/prometheus.go:4]\n224\t- **Evaluation job orchestration:** When an evaluation is submitted, the server creates Kubernetes batch Jobs via `KubernetesHelper.CreateJob` (`k8s_helper.go:157-161`), with associated ConfigMaps for evaluation configuration and Secrets for credentials. The `eval_runtime_init` init container downloads test data from S3-compatible storage using the AWS SDK. The `eval_runtime_sidecar` proxies requests between the evaluation runtime and the main service. HardwareProfile CRs are queried to support hardware-aware scheduling of evaluation workloads. [source: internal/eval_hub/runtimes/k8s/k8s_helper.go:112-232, cmd/eval_runtime_init/main.go:114]\n225\t- **External integrations:** The service optionally connects to an MLflow Tracking Server over HTTPS with TLS 1.2-1.3 and custom CA certificate support for experiment tracking (`mlflow.go:43-92`). Traces, metrics, and logs are exported to an OpenTelemetry Collector over OTLP/gRPC (`internal/otel/otel_sdk.go:174`). The evalhub_mcp component exposes a Model Context Protocol server for AI agent integration. [source: internal/eval_hub/mlflow/mlflow.go:24-92, internal/otel/otel_sdk.go:174, internal/evalhub_mcp/server/server.go:223-228]\n226\t- **Security context:** 7 authentication rules describe enforcement across API endpoints and the Kubernetes API. Identity headers are conditionally required based on runtime configuration. Kubernetes operations use kubeconfig credential chains. TLS configuration imports are present across 10 source files for both HTTP and gRPC transports. [source: internal/eval_hub/server/server.go:430-441, internal/eval_hub/runtimes/k8s/k8s_helper.go:41]\n227\t\n228\t## Integration Points\n229\t\n230\t- **/v1/ConfigMap:** Resource CRUD; purpose: create operations by KubernetesHelper. [source: cmd/eval_runtime_init/main.go:52, 114, go.mod, internal/eval_hub/runtimes/k8s/k8s_helper.go:41, 112, 153, 161, 232, internal/otel/otel_sdk.go:174]\n231\t- **/v1/Secret:** Resource CRUD; purpose: create operations by KubernetesHelper. [source: cmd/eval_runtime_init/main.go:52, 114, go.mod, internal/eval_hub/runtimes/k8s/k8s_helper.go:41, 112, 153, 161, 232, internal/otel/otel_sdk.go:174]\n232\t- **HardwareProfile CR:** CRD CRUD; purpose: Manage hardware profile resources. [source: cmd/eval_runtime_init/main.go:52, 114, go.mod, internal/eval_hub/runtimes/k8s/k8s_helper.go:41, 112, 153, 161, 232, i