{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a63a21d3-aea4-4f1f-9448-a7fb6d26319b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8f5d73c90b530f5e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-6ln7i5f7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E003.md","content":"# EvalHub Evaluations page auto-refresh polling layer and state differentiation\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the real-time state visibility foundation for the EvalHub Evaluations landing page in the RHOAI dashboard: a two-layer polling architecture (the existing 30-second list-endpoint polling plus a new 10-second detail-polling layer for in-progress jobs), round-robin concurrency control capped at 5 concurrent requests, Page Visibility API pause/resume, non-blocking error handling with retry and exponential backoff, and visual differentiation of queued/pending, running, failed, and completed job states.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Detail-polling layer in the eval-hub-ui plugin that identifies jobs on the currently displayed table page in a non-terminal state and fetches GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id} on a 10-second cycle, following the React Query retry-with-backoff pattern established by the autorag package (`placeholderData` preserving the last successful response, exponential backoff with jitter, 4xx errors non-retryable, 5xx/network errors retried).\n- Concurrency control: maximum 5 concurrent detail requests per user session, dispatched round-robin so the next pending job is fetched as one completes; a 10-second timer starts when all detail fetches for the current page complete; only jobs visible on the current table page (client-side pagination, 5/10/20 rows) are polled, with polling targets updating immediately when the table page changes.\n- Page Visibility API integration: polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded and resumes with an immediate single polling cycle when the tab regains focus.\n- Error handling: a non-blocking inline warning (PatternFly Alert variant \"warning\") indicating that status updates are temporarily unavailable while continuing to display the last successfully fetched data; a failed detail request does not stop the round-robin — partial progress data is acceptable.\n- State visual differentiation driven by the list endpoint's `status.state` field (available for all jobs without detail fetch): distinct PatternFly label, icon, and color for queued/pending, running, failed (with `status.message` providing error context), and completed; state badge transitions appear without manual refresh within the list polling interval.\n- Graceful degradation: if the detail endpoint is unavailable, rows show only top-level state from the list endpoint; the existing list-endpoint polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged (the change is additive).\n- Validation of the retry-with-backoff pattern in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context by simulating 5xx errors from the BFF proxy.\n- Verification that the odh-dashboard BFF proxy passes through all response fields from the eval-hub-ui plugin backend without filtering (existing behavior; no BFF code change expected).\n- State icon, color, and label specifications reviewed by UX/Design.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job transitions from running to complete, when the user is on the Evaluations landing page without manually refreshing the browser, then the job row's state badge updates automatically within the list endpoint's 30-second polling interval.\n- Given an evaluation job is queued/pending, when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct \"Queued\" label, icon, and color treatment visually distinguishable from Running, Failed, and Completed, per the PatternFly status pattern.\n- Given the EvalHub Server is temporarily unreachable during detail polling (5xx or network error on a detail fetch), then the last successfully fetched data for the affected job remains displayed, a non-blocking inline warning Alert is visible, the failed request retries with exponential backoff (up to 5 retries; 4xx errors not retried), and the round-robin continues with the next in-progress job.\n- Given the user navigates away from the browser tab, then no requests are made to the detail endpoint while the tab is backgrounded, and a single polling cycle triggers immediately when the tab regains focus (verified via browser dev tools Network tab).\n- At most 5 detail requests are in flight concurrently per user session regardless of how many jobs on the current page are in progress, and only jobs on the currently displayed table page are polled.\n- When all detail fetches for the current page complete, the next polling cycle starts after a 10-second timer.\n- The retry-with-backoff pattern is validated in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context against simulated 5xx responses from the BFF proxy.\n- The odh-dashboard BFF proxy is verified to pass through all response fields from the eval-hub-ui plugin backend without filtering.\n- State icon, color, and label specifications are reviewed and approved by UX/Design.\n- The existing list-endpoint polling and table rendering continue to function unchanged with the detail-polling layer active.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P0] Auto-refresh mechanism for the Evaluations landing page job list showing state transitions without manual refresh, using existing list-endpoint polling for top-level state and new detail-endpoint polling for in-progress job progress\n- [P0] Visual distinction between queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states with distinct labels, icons, and color treatments derived from the list endpoint's `status.state` field\n- [P0] Non-blocking error handling during detail polling: last successful state preserved, inline warning displayed, retry with exponential backoff per the autorag pattern\n- [P1] Polling pauses when the browser tab is not in the foreground (Page Visibility API) and resumes immediately on tab focus\n- [P1] Max-5 concurrent round-robin fetch for in-progress jobs on the current table page (polling-layer portion)\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74594,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-854fba31643c93bf","agent_id":"a60c1c46c7da11595","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"1ae54d73-c7bd-488d-ba3e-2e9d8a598a40","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:54:36.611Z","subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8005"}
