{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-a63a21d3-aea4-4f1f-9448-a7fb6d26319b","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-a506feee2b736c49","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8005-6ln7i5f7/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8005-E004.md","content":"# Benchmark progress and elapsed time display for running evaluation jobs\n\n## Description\n\nDelivers the progress display for running evaluation jobs on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page: benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array, and elapsed time computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps (falling back to `resource.created_at` before any benchmark has started). This work consumes the detail-polling data layer introduced for the Evaluations landing page and is gated on the validated availability of benchmark status data mid-run.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs: the count of `status.benchmarks[]` entries with `status: \"completed\"` over the total number of benchmarks (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 2/5 complete\").\n- Elapsed time display computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp across benchmarks (or `resource.created_at` if no benchmark has started); per-benchmark duration is available where both `started_at` and `completed_at` are present.\n- Until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, only the top-level state from the list endpoint is shown for that job (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n- Elapsed time serves as the primary progress indicator for all jobs, with the benchmark count supplementary — including single-benchmark jobs, where the count alone can only show 0 or 1 complete (strategy risk mitigation).\n- Progress indicator pattern reviewed by UX/Design; the strategy notes a progress indicator UX specification is to be created.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id} response.\n- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response (or `resource.created_at` before any benchmark has started).\n- Given no detail fetch has yet returned for a job, then only the top-level state from the list endpoint is displayed for that job.\n- For single-benchmark jobs, elapsed time is displayed as the primary progress indicator.\n- The progress indicator pattern is reviewed by UX/Design.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 2/5 complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array (display portion; the round-robin fetch layer is delivered with the polling foundation)\n- [P1] Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps obtained via detail polling\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":74594,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-854fba31643c93bf","agent_id":"a60c1c46c7da11595","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"233a78e6-4de6-4ff8-9116-93d7485da88e","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:54:44.216Z","subagent_type"