{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-92df7fad8a7fe901","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n3\tepic_count: 5\n4\tcritical_path_length: 2\n5\tdecompose_complete: true\n6\trevised: false\n7\ttriage: null\n8\ttriage_rationale: null\n9\t---\n10\t# Decomposition Summary: RHAISTRAT-8005 — EvalHub UI: Real-Time Evaluation Job Progress and State Visibility\n11\t\n12\t## Triage Outcome\n13\t\n14\tThe strategy is S-sized, frontend-only, and owned by a single implementation team — but it carries two\n15\topen questions explicitly marked \"needs validation\" whose answers change what downstream epics do\n16\t(whether benchmark-level progress can be displayed mid-run, and whether pre-start failures can be\n17\tdistinguished from runtime failures). The genuine-unknowns escape condition therefore applies and the\n18\tstrategy is fully decomposed rather than collapsed to a single below-threshold epic.\n19\t\n20\t## Epic List\n21\t\n22\t| ID | Title | Type | Team | Priority |\n23\t|----|-------|------|------|----------|\n24\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E001 | Investigate mid-run availability of benchmark status in the EvalHub job detail API | Investigation | TrustyAI / EvalHub | P1 |\n25\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E002 | Investigate message_code values distinguishing pre-start from runtime evaluation failures | Investigation | TrustyAI / EvalHub | P2 |\n26\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E003 | EvalHub Evaluations page auto-refresh polling layer and state differentiation | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P0 |\n27\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E004 | Benchmark progress and elapsed time display for running evaluation jobs | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P1 |\n28\t| RHAISTRAT-8005-E005 | Pre-start versus runtime failure distinction in the evaluations job list | Implementation | ODH Dashboard | P2 |\n29\t\n30\t## Dependency DAG\n31\t\n32\t```mermaid\n33\tgraph TD\n34\t    E001[\"E001 Inv: benchmarks[] mid-run availability\"] --> E004[\"E004 Impl: progress + elapsed display\"]\n35\t    E002[\"E002 Inv: message_code failure classes\"] --> E005[\"E005 Impl: pre-start vs runtime failure\"]\n36\t    E003[\"E003 Impl: polling layer + state differentiation\"] --> E004\n37\t    E003 --> E005\n38\t```\n39\t\n40\tRoots: E001, E002, E003 (all three can start immediately). Critical path length: 2 epics.\n41\t\n42\t## DAG Justification\n43\t\n44\t| Edge | Rule | Rationale |\n45\t|------|------|-----------|\n46\t| E001 → E004 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementation) | Whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated mid-run determines the scope of the progress display: if only populated on completion, the epic is rewritten to elapsed-time-primary. True gate, `gate_failure_impact.action=rewrite`. |\n47\t| E002 → E005 | Rule 3 (Investigation gates affected Implementation) | Whether `message_code` values reliably distinguish pre-start from runtime failures determines whether the P2 distinction feature exists at all. True gate, `gate_failure_impact.action=remove` (fallback: single Failed state with `status.message` text, already provided by the core state differentiation). |\n48\t| E003 → E004 | Rule 13 (producer artifact → consumer serial) | The progress/elapsed display builds directly against the detail-polling hook and its fetched data (`status.benchmarks[]`, `started_at`), produced by the polling-layer epic. |\n49\t| E003 → E005 | Rule 12/13 (framework → consumer) | The failure distinction refines the failed-state rendering (label/icon/color per state) established by the state differentiation work. |\n50\t| No edge E001/E002 → E003 | — | Neither unknown affects the P0 core: list-endpoint state display, the polling mechanics, concurrency cap, retry, and page-visibility behavior are identical under every outcome. P0 work is not blocked by either investigation. |\n51\t| No edge E004 ↔ E005 | Rule 14/15 (independent surfaces) | Progress display and failure-state distinction touch different aspects of the job row and share no artifacts beyond the shared P0 foundation. |\n52\t\n53\t## HLR Traceability Matrix\n54\t\n55\t| HLR | Priority | Epic(s) |\n56\t|-----|----------|---------|\n57\t| HLR-1: Auto-refresh mechanism for the Evaluations landing page (list polling for top-level state + detail polling for in-progress job progress) | P0 | E003 |\n58\t| HLR-2: Visual distinction between queued/pending, running, failed, and completed states (labels, icons, colors from `status.state`) | P0 | E003, E005 |\n59\t| HLR-3: Non-blocking error handling during detail polling (last state preserved, inline warning, exponential backoff retry) | P0 | E003 |\n60\t| HLR-4: Benchmark-level progress display (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") with max-5 concurrent round-robin fetch for in-progress jobs on the current page | P1 | E003 (round-robin fetch layer), E004 (progress display) |\n61\t| HLR-5: Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` | P1 | E004 |\n62\t| HLR-6: Polling pauses when the browser tab is backgrounded (Page Visibility API), resumes immediately on focus | P1 | E003 |\n63\t| HLR-7: Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` | P2 | E005 |\n64\t\n65\tAll seven HLRs are covered; no orphaned requirements. HLR-4 is split across E003/E004 along the\n66\tdata-layer/display boundary: the P0 auto-refresh HLR already requires the detail-polling mechanism\n67\t(including the NFR-mandated 5-concurrent cap), so the polling layer lives in the P0 epic and the\n68\tdisplay consumes it.\n69\t\n70\t## Staff Engineer Input Overrides\n71\t\n72\tThe Staff Engineer Input section is non-empty and takes precedence. Logged divergences/adoptions:\n73\t\n74\t1. **Data availability constraint** — Staff direction: assume no data beyond what the two existing\n75\t   API endpoints provide. Adopted throughout; no Server-side extension epics are generated\n76\t   (consistent with the strategy's out-of-scope list).\n77\t2. **Polling design specifics** — 10-second detail cycle, max 5 parallel requests in round-robin,\n78\t   only jobs on the currently displayed page (client-side pagination, 5/10/20 rows), timer starts\n79\t   when all fetches complete, retry-with-backoff per the autorag pattern. All adopted verbatim into\n80\t   the P0 polling-layer epic scope.\n81\t3. **Open questions answered by Staff** — 10-second latency window sufficient; Page Visibility API\n82\t   pause yes; poll only in-view jobs; no scalability consideration this release. Adopted; the\n83\t   scalability deferral is respected (no performance-optimization epic).\n84\t4. **Open questions NOT answered by Staff** — the two Open Questions table items (mid-run\n85\t   `status.benchmarks[]` population; `message_code` value enumeration) remain genuine unknowns and\n86\t   are modeled as Investigations E001/E002 rather than downgraded to implementation details.\n87\t\n88\t## Component Mapping\n89\t\n90\t- `eval-hub-ui (odh-dashboard plugin)` → canonical component **AI Core Dashboard** (the plugin lives\n91\t  in the odh-dashboard monorepo; the canonical list has no eval-hub-ui entry — non-obvious mapping\n92\t  logged here).\n93\t- EvalHub Server API behavior questions (E001/E002) → canonical component **AI Evaluations**.\n94\t- `odh-dashboard (BFF)` is **passive** (\"verify proxy passthrough — no code change expected\") and is\n95\t  owned by the same team as the active component, so per Step 2 its validation is an acceptance\n96\t  criterion on E003, not a separate epic.\n97\t- UX/Design involvement (state icon/color specs, progress indicator pattern review) is review\n98\t  support, not a separate work stream; it is captured as acceptance criteria on the implementation\n99\t  epics. No substantive docs/content authoring is in scope, so no `docs-authoring` epic is generated.\n100\t\n101\t## Investigation Outcomes and Conditional Handling\n102\t\n103\tBoth investigations have two bounded outcomes each. Neither outcome changes which epics exist or the\n104\tDAG shape — only the internal scope of the gated epic changes — so conditional branch files are not\n105\twarranted; the outcomes are captured via `gated_by` + `gate_failure_impact` on the gated epics:\n106\t\n107\t- **E001 outcomes**: (a) `status.benchmarks[]` populated mid-run → E004 as planned; (b) populated\n108\t  only on completion → E004 rewritten: elapsed time (from `resource.created_at` fallback) becomes\n109\t  the primary progress indicator, benchmark count shown only where available.\n110\t- **E002 outcomes**: (a) `message_code` values distinguish failure classes → E005 as planned;\n111\t  (b) indistinguishable → E005 removed; fallback is the single \"Failed\" state with\n112\t  `status.message` text as supplementary detail (already delivered by the core state\n113\t  differentiation in E003).\n114\t\n115\t## Health Warnings\n116\t\n117\t- **Human process gates pending**: every entry in the strategy's Prerequisites & Process Gates\n118\t  table (Architecture Review, Licence Validation, UXD Support, Performance Team Support) is\n119\t  \"Pending human review\". These are schedule/approval risks outside epic scope; UXD review is\n120\t  folded in as acceptance criteria where the strategy requires it.\n121\t- **Proposed ACs unvalidated**: the strategy's acceptance criteria are marked \"requires\n122\t  PM/Engineering validation\".\n123\t- **Coarse progress granularity risk**: for jobs with few benchmarks (e.g., a single benchmark),\n124\t  \"X/N complete\" shows only 0 or 1; the strategy's mitigation (elapsed time as primary indicator)\n125\t  is carried as an acceptance criterion on E004.\n126\t- **Design doc without an owner**: the strategy lists \"progress indicator UX specification — to be\n127\t  created\" with no assigned author; treated as UXD-reviewed specifications within the\n128\t  implementation epics rather than a separate work stream. If substantive design-doc authoring is\n129\t  later required, it should be re-planned.\n130\t- **Unvalidated retry-pattern assumption**: the autorag React Query retry pattern has not been\n131\t  exercised in the eval-hub-ui Module Federation context with per-job detail fetching; validation\n132\t  against simulated 5xx responses is an acceptance criterion on E003 (fix-and-retry, not a\n133\t  scope-changing unknown).\n134\t\n135\t## Tiered Delivery\n136\t\n137\tNot applicable — all internal and external dependencies (BFF proxy path, EvalHub Server endpoints,\n138\tPatternFly, React Query) have status \"Exists\"; no dependency has uncertain timing.\n139\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b697caef81f58110","agent_id":"a5deb79688eac204b","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"bf7fff90-32ba-4228-a6d5-5b10b8eebcc8","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:57:06.893Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-92df7fad8a7fe901","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
