{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d05f5cef8009151","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n3\ttitle: Investigate mid-run availability of benchmark status in the EvalHub job detail\n4\t  API\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P1\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigate mid-run availability of benchmark status in the EvalHub job detail API\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolves whether the EvalHub Server's job detail endpoint (GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id}) populates the `status.benchmarks[]` array with per-benchmark status entries while an evaluation job is still running, or only after the job completes. The answer determines whether benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") can be displayed mid-run on the Evaluations landing page, or whether elapsed time must serve as the primary progress indicator with the benchmark count shown only where available.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Inspect the EvalHub Server source code and published API documentation to determine when per-benchmark status entries (`started_at`, `completed_at`, per-benchmark `status`) are written to `status.benchmarks[]` during job execution.\n35\t- Where feasible, corroborate the source analysis with an observed detail-endpoint response from a running evaluation job.\n36\t- Document which fields are present mid-run and the point in the job lifecycle at which entries appear.\n37\t- Recommend the progress-display approach the UI should take if benchmark counts prove unavailable mid-run (elapsed time as the primary indicator, per the strategy's risk mitigation).\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A written determination states whether `status.benchmarks[]` is populated with per-benchmark status entries while a job is running or only upon completion, citing EvalHub Server source locations and/or observed API responses as evidence.\n42\t- If populated mid-run, the fields available mid-run (per-benchmark status, `started_at`, `completed_at`) are documented.\n43\t- A recommendation for the progress-display approach is produced, sufficient to finalize the scope of the benchmark progress and elapsed time display work.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array (determines feasibility and shape of that display)\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b697caef81f58110","agent_id":"a5deb79688eac204b","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"81c00883-c4cf-490e-b02a-84c4479144f3","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:57:10.867Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8d05f5cef8009151","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
