{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-807c26e7938cd6f5","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n3\ttitle: Investigate message_code values distinguishing pre-start from runtime evaluation\n4\t  failures\n5\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n6\tcomponent: AI Evaluations\n7\tteam: TrustyAI / EvalHub\n8\ttype: Investigation\n9\tpriority: P2\n10\tinvestigation_signals:\n11\t  question_specificity: 1\n12\t  source_accessibility: 1\n13\t  local_runnability: 0\n14\t  cluster_hardware_dependence: -1\n15\t  human_judgment_required: 0\n16\timplementation_type: null\n17\tdependencies: []\n18\tai_signals: null\n19\tai_implementability: Medium\n20\tai_implementability_score: 1\n21\tjira_key: null\n22\tbranch: null\n23\tgated_by: null\n24\tgate_failure_impact: null\n25\t---\n26\t# Investigate message_code values distinguishing pre-start from runtime evaluation failures\n27\t\n28\t## Description\n29\t\n30\tResolves what values the EvalHub Server's `status.message.message_code` field takes for pre-start failures (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource quota or constraint errors) versus runtime failures during benchmark execution. The answer determines whether the Evaluations job list can reliably render \"Failed (not started)\" as a visual treatment distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state, or whether a single Failed state with message text must be used.\n31\t\n32\t## Scope\n33\t\n34\t- Inspect the EvalHub Server source code to enumerate the `message_code` values emitted for admission errors, scheduling failures, and resource constraints, and those emitted for runtime errors during benchmark execution.\n35\t- Where feasible, corroborate the source analysis with observed failure responses.\n36\t- Document a mapping of `message_code` values (or ranges/prefixes) to pre-start versus runtime failure classes, or conclude that no reliable distinction exists.\n37\t- Recommend whether the pre-start/runtime failure distinction is implementable, and the fallback treatment (single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text as supplementary detail) if it is not.\n38\t\n39\t## Acceptance Criteria\n40\t\n41\t- A written enumeration of `message_code` values per failure class (pre-start vs runtime) exists, with EvalHub Server source citations.\n42\t- A determination states whether the values reliably distinguish pre-start from runtime failures across error scenarios, including cases where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent.\n43\t- If the distinction is not reliable, the recommended fallback treatment is documented.\n44\t\n45\t## HLR Traceability\n46\t\n47\t- [P2] Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available (determines feasibility and existence of that distinction)\n48\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b697caef81f58110","agent_id":"a5deb79688eac204b","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"3680b89f-29f0-44a7-9d2a-49692e17ce79","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:57:11.536Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-807c26e7938cd6f5","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
