{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba91037199a94b9e","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E005\n3\ttitle: Pre-start versus runtime failure distinction in the evaluations job list\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P2\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E002\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If message_code values cannot reliably distinguish pre-start\n16\t    from runtime failures, drop the distinction and use a single Failed state with\n17\t    status.message text as supplementary detail (already provided by the core state\n18\t    differentiation work).\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n23\t  existing_foundation: 1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 1\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: High\n32\tai_implementability_score: 4\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\tbranch: null\n35\t---\n36\t# Pre-start versus runtime failure distinction in the evaluations job list\n37\t\n38\t## Description\n39\t\n40\tExtends the failed-state rendering on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page to distinguish jobs that failed before execution started (admission errors, scheduling failures, resource constraints) from jobs that ran and then failed, using `status.message.message_code` where available. Builds on the state differentiation (labels, icons, colors) established for the job list and is gated on the validated enumeration of message_code values for the two failure classes.\n41\t\n42\t## Scope\n43\t\n44\t- Mapping from `status.message.message_code` values to a \"Failed (not started)\" treatment versus a runtime \"Failed\" treatment, using the validated enumeration of message_code values for pre-start failures (admission error, scheduling failure, resource constraint).\n45\t- Distinct label, icon, and color for \"Failed (not started)\" versus \"Failed\", consistent with the PatternFly status pattern and the UXD-reviewed state specifications.\n46\t- Fallback where `message_code` is ambiguous or absent: a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text displayed as supplementary detail.\n47\t\n48\t## Acceptance Criteria\n49\t\n50\t- Given an evaluation job failed before execution started (e.g., admission error indicated by `status.message.message_code`), when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row displays a distinct visual treatment (e.g., \"Failed (not started)\") with a label, icon, and color distinct from the runtime \"Failed\" state.\n51\t- Given an evaluation job failed during execution, when a user views the Evaluations landing page, then the job row renders the runtime \"Failed\" treatment.\n52\t- Given `message_code` is ambiguous or absent for a failed job, then the job row falls back to a single \"Failed\" state with `status.message` text displayed as supplementary detail.\n53\t- The new visual treatments are reviewed against the UXD state icon/color specifications.\n54\t\n55\t## HLR Traceability\n56\t\n57\t- [P2] Pre-start vs. runtime failure distinction using `status.message.message_code` where available\n58\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b697caef81f58110","agent_id":"a5deb79688eac204b","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"24f34e6a-bcb4-44ee-a907-c54336d20c3c","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:57:19.097Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ba91037199a94b9e","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-8005 decomposition"}
