{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae7760f4e074d1f3","type":"tool_result","content":"196:#### Investigation epics → `investigation_signals` (5 signals)\n197-\n198:**Do not use the 9 Implementation signals for Investigation epics.** Those penalize the *defining* traits of an investigation (open questions, no prior foundation, external dependency), so they mis-route nearly every investigation to Low — even ones the AI resolves easily. Instead score these five, which predict whether the AI investigation skill can resolve the unknowns (→ assign to the skill) or a person must (→ assign to a person). Write the values into `investigation_signals`.\n199-\n200-| # | Signal | Frontmatter key | Range | How to score |\n201-|---|--------|-----------------|-------|--------------|\n202-| 1 | Question specificity | `question_specificity` | -1 / 0 / +1 | +1 concrete, enumerable questions with a defined pass/fail criterion; -1 vague or criterion undefined (a human must frame it first) |\n203-| 2 | Source accessibility | `source_accessibility` | 0 / +1 | +1 a readable artifact that **contains or determines the answer** exists (open repo, docs, public record). 0 when the only readable material does **not** hold the answer — e.g. a decision/PR still under review (the answer doesn't exist yet) |\n204-| 3 | Local runnability | `local_runnability` | 0 / +1 | +1 the components can be exercised as a downloaded **binary or pip/npm library** locally — including backing a datastore with an embedded/bundled server (e.g. `pgserver` for PostgreSQL). 0 only if it genuinely can't run without a container/cluster |\n205-| 4 | Cluster/hardware dependence | `cluster_hardware_dependence` | -2 / -1 / 0 | 0 none. -1 some *peripheral* questions need a live cluster / GPU / prod-scale. -2 a *gating* question does. **What an operator/controller _generates_** (rendered CR, template, NetworkPolicy, RBAC in its source repo) is readable source — score it under `source_accessibility`, **not** here; only the *as-deployed runtime state* of a live cluster counts as a dependence |\n206-| 5 | Human judgment required | `human_judgment_required` | -2 / -1 / 0 | 0 none. -1 a *peripheral* question needs a stakeholder/product decision or external-party input. -2 the *gating* question is itself a human/governance decision or external coordination the AI cannot make (e.g. \"is this ADR approved?\") |\n207-\n208-The pipeline routes: **High** → assign to the investigation skill; **Medium** → hybrid (skill resolves the desk/local parts and hands a spec to a human for the rest); **Low** → assign to a person.\n209-\n210-Write the signal rationale to a separate file `artifacts/epic-tasks/{ID}-ENNN-ai-signals.md` (one per epic), for whichever signal set you used. Format as a markdown table with Signal, Value, and Rationale columns. Do not write the signals table into the epic body.\n211-\n212-## Step 6.5: Health Warnings\n213-\n214-### Non-blocking warnings (decomposition proceeds, human verifies later)\n215-- Priority inversions (P0/P1/P2 inconsistent with technical complexity/reliability)\n216-- Scope traps: ACs implying infrastructure that doesn't exist, contradictions between out-of-scope items and NFRs, storage beyond design intent\n217-\n218-### Handling unclear strategy passages\n219-\n220-When the strategy is unclear about something, apply this two-way distinction:\n221-\n222-| Situation | Handling |\n223-|-----------|---------|\n224-| **Implementation detail** — the team will resolve this when they start the work (version choices, API surface discovery, config decisions, validation of assumptions) | Not a flag. Capture as an AC on the relevant epic if needed. Most unclear passages fall here. |\n225-| **Genuine unknown** — nobody knows yet, resolution requires technical work, and the answer changes which downstream epics exist or what they do | Investigation epic with conditional downstream epics. |\n226-\n227-When a strategy explicitly flags something as an open question, pending review, or conditional ADR, treat it as a genuine unknown — the strategy author has already classified it. Do not downgrade to an implementation detail based on descriptive text elsewhere in the strategy. A detailed description of current state is context, not a decision. If the strategy indicates the resolution could require a different approach (conditional ADRs, \"if X requires changes to Y\"), evaluate which downstream epics build on the current assumption and gate them on the resolution.\n228-\n--\n309:`investigation_signals` instead of `ai_signals` (do not set both):\n310-\n311-```bash\n312-python3 scripts/frontmatter.py set artifacts/epic-tasks/{ID}-E001.md \\\n313-    epic_id=\"{ID}-E001\" title=\"<epic title>\" parent_strat=\"{ID}\" \\\n314-    component=\"<canonical name>\" team=\"<owner team>\" \\\n315-    type=Investigation priority=P0 \\\n316:    investigation_signals.question_specificity=1 \\\n317:    investigation_signals.source_accessibility=1 \\\n318:    investigation_signals.local_runnability=1 \\\n319:    investigation_signals.cluster_hardware_dependence=0 \\\n320:    investigation_signals.human_judgment_required=0\n321-```\n322-\n323-Add optional fields only when non-null: `implementation_type=<value>`, `branch=<value>`, `gated_by=<epic_id>`, `gate_failure_impact.action=<value> gate_failure_impact.fallback_approach=\"<text>\"`. Every epic that depends on an Investigation should have `gated_by` pointing to that Investigation (see Rule 3).\n324-\n325:Do **not** include `ai_implementability` or `ai_implementability_score` — the pipeline computes those from `ai_signals` (Implementation) or `investigation_signals` (Investigation) automatically.\n326-\n327-### Step 8c: Verify consistency\n328-\n329-After writing all epic files, run:\n330-```\n331-python3 scripts/frontmatter.py batch-read artifacts/epic-tasks/{ID}-*E[0-9][0-9][0-9].md\n332-```\n333-\n334-Compare the output against the decomposition summary. If any epic file's `dependencies`, `priority`, `type`, or HLR mappings diverged from the plan, fix the epic file to match the summary.\n335-\n336-Then run the contract validator until it passes:\n337-\n338-```bash\n339-python3 skills/epic-decompose/scripts/validate_decomposition.py {ID}\n340-```\n341-\n342-It deterministically checks what downstream consumers enforce and an LLM step can silently get wrong: epic body sections (Description / Scope / Acceptance Criteria / HLR Traceability), `component` values verbatim in `.context/rhai-components.txt`, Rule 11 (docs-authoring blocked by every Implementation epic), and priority inheritance (an epic blocking P0 work is itself P0). It prints one `VIOLATION:` line per problem and exits non-zero. Fix every violation by editing the epic files (never edit the script), re-run, and proceed only once it prints `OK`.\n343-\n344-Then, as your **final action** — after every epic file is written, any divergence is fixed, and the validator prints `OK` — mark the decomposition complete:\n345-\n346-```\n347-python3 scripts/frontmatter.py set artifacts/epic-tasks/{ID}-decomposition.md decompose_complete=true\n348-```\n349-\n350-The pipeline uses this field to detect that you have finished. Until it is set, the review agent is not launched. Do not set it earlier: anything you write or edit after setting it may be reviewed in a partially written state.\n351-\n352-### Conditional decomposition (when applicable)\n353-\n354-If an Investigation epic has ≤3 bounded outcomes that change downstream structure, write one file per branch epic using the `-BRANCH-<letter>-` filename convention:","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b697caef81f58110","agent_id":"a5deb79688eac204b","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"de6240f9-fdfa-4822-808f-f3e6add75578","timestamp":"2026-10-22T04:59:02.275Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-ae7760f4e074d1f3","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","rea