153\treview-approval ACs are binary and verifiable. No epic body references sibling epics by\n154\tdraft ID (grep confirmed; dependencies use full epic IDs only in frontmatter, where they\n155\tbelong).\n156\t\n157\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n158\t\n159\tThe combined epic set accounts for the full strategy scope: two-layer polling,\n160\tconcurrency control, progress model, retry-on-error, Page Visibility, state\n161\tdifferentiation, BFF passthrough verification, and the P2 failure distinction. All\n162\tstrategy-level context is carried forward: the four risks map to concrete epic scope/ACs\n163\t(coarse-progress → elapsed-time-primary in E004; message_code ambiguity → E005 fallback;\n164\tscalability → deferred per Staff direction; retry-pattern risk → E003 validation AC); both\n165\topen questions are modeled as Investigations E001/E002 rather than downgraded; Staff\n166\tEngineer Input overrides are explicitly logged and respected (no server-extension epics,\n167\tpolling specifics adopted verbatim, scalability deferral honored). Out-of-scope items are\n168\trespected — no epics for push infrastructure, notifications, log access, or server API\n169\tchanges.\n170\t\n171\tConditional handling covers both bounded outcomes for each investigation with concrete\n172\tfallback approaches. Documentation Support in the Prerequisites table is \"Pending human\n173\treview,\" not \"Yes,\" and the strategy contains no documentation deliverable in scope, so\n174\tthe absence of a docs-authoring epic is correct (Rule 11 trigger not met); the summary\n175\tdocuments this reasoning and the Health Warnings flag the pending human gates. The\n176\tpending-UXD-support and unvalidated-AC risks are surfaced in Health Warnings rather than\n177\tsilently dropped.\n178\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-83c29e8e90ee569f","agent_id":"a23244b2981b2a888","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"4e5fbae2-26e8-4388-86fc-4ea988ea9799","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:01:1