{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7fcfa805096e337","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8005-E004\n3\ttitle: Benchmark progress and elapsed time display for running evaluation jobs\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8005\n5\tcomponent: AI Core Dashboard\n6\tteam: ODH Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tdependencies:\n10\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n11\t- RHAISTRAT-8005-E003\n12\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8005-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: rewrite\n15\t  fallback_approach: If status.benchmarks[] is only populated after job completion,\n16\t    rework to elapsed time as the primary progress indicator (computed from resource.created_at)\n17\t    and show benchmark counts only where the detail response provides them.\n18\tai_signals:\n19\t  change_specificity: 1\n20\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n21\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n22\t  existing_foundation: 1\n23\t  open_questions: -1\n24\t  external_dependency: 1\n25\t  human_process_gates: -1\n26\t  repo_access: 1\n27\t  architecture_claims: 1\n28\timplementation_type: null\n29\tinvestigation_signals: null\n30\tai_implementability: High\n31\tai_implementability_score: 5\n32\tjira_key: null\n33\tbranch: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Benchmark progress and elapsed time display for running evaluation jobs\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tDelivers the progress display for running evaluation jobs on the EvalHub Evaluations landing page: benchmark-level progress (\"Benchmarks: X/N complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array, and elapsed time computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps (falling back to `resource.created_at` before any benchmark has started). This work consumes the detail-polling data layer introduced for the Evaluations landing page and is gated on the validated availability of benchmark status data mid-run.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs: the count of `status.benchmarks[]` entries with `status: \"completed\"` over the total number of benchmarks (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 2/5 complete\").\n44\t- Elapsed time display computed client-side as the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp across benchmarks (or `resource.created_at` if no benchmark has started); per-benchmark duration is available where both `started_at` and `completed_at` are present.\n45\t- Until the first detail fetch returns for a given job, only the top-level state from the list endpoint is shown for that job (no benchmark progress or elapsed time).\n46\t- Elapsed time serves as the primary progress indicator for all jobs, with the benchmark count supplementary — including single-benchmark jobs, where the count alone can only show 0 or 1 complete (strategy risk mitigation).\n47\t- Progress indicator pattern reviewed by UX/Design; the strategy notes a progress indicator UX specification is to be created.\n48\t\n49\t## Acceptance Criteria\n50\t\n51\t- Given an evaluation job is in the running state with 3 of 5 benchmarks completed, when a user views the Evaluations landing page and the detail-polling cycle has completed for that job, then benchmark-level progress is displayed (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 3/5 complete\"), measured by the count matching the number of entries in the `status.benchmarks[]` array with `status: \"completed\"` in the GET /api/v1/evaluations/jobs/{id} response.\n52\t- Given an evaluation job has been running for 4 minutes, when the detail-polling cycle has fetched the job's detail endpoint, then elapsed time is displayed (e.g., \"Elapsed: 4m 12s\"), measured by the elapsed time being the difference between the current time and the earliest per-benchmark `started_at` timestamp in the detail response (or `resource.created_at` before any benchmark has started).\n53\t- Given no detail fetch has yet returned for a job, then only the top-level state from the list endpoint is displayed for that job.\n54\t- For single-benchmark jobs, elapsed time is displayed as the primary progress indicator.\n55\t- The progress indicator pattern is reviewed by UX/Design.\n56\t\n57\t## HLR Traceability\n58\t\n59\t- [P1] Benchmark-level progress display for running jobs (e.g., \"Benchmarks: 2/5 complete\") derived from the detail endpoint's `status.benchmarks[]` array (display portion; the round-robin fetch layer is delivered with the polling foundation)\n60\t- [P1] Elapsed time display for running jobs, computed client-side from per-benchmark `started_at` timestamps obtained via detail polling\n61\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-833851858ad1b676","agent_id":"ac4267778db008f3e","session_id":"6801b43c-a805-4fcb-88e0-698d74311470","uuid":"8783fce3-3094-472b-858c-e50547a542ee","timestamp":"2026-10-22T05:02:40.972Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7fcfa805096e337","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"claude","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8005"}
